Package: flickos-layouts
Architecture: all
# flickos-settings: its rc.xml, foot, fuzzel and mako configs are the base of
# the overlay, its panel the fallback, and it has the FlickOS-Arc window theme.
# 1.10: its rc.xml binds the default desktop clicks (DEFAULT_CLICKS). 1.17: the
# default button-layout that layouts without TitlebarLayout reset to.
# libglib2.0-bin: gsettings (icon theme for pinned apps, button-layout) and gio
# launch (dock clicks).
# python3-gi, gir1.2-gtk-3.0: the chooser window (flickos-layout pick), GTK 3 so
# it follows the Arc theme.
# sfwbar: the Cupertino dock and Traditional's window list (Dock=). +flickos3
# has the .running class dock.css uses and sensor_maximized; +flickos4 marks
# the current desktop in Traditional's desktop switcher.
Depends: flickos-branding (>= 1.4),
         python3,
         python3-gi,
         gir1.2-gtk-3.0,
         libglib2.0-bin,
         flickos-settings (>= 1.17),
         sfwbar (>= 1.0~beta17+git20260910+flickos4),
         ${misc:Depends}
# flick-tiler 1.1 tells waybar when the tiling state changes (SIGRTMIN+8);
# 1.7 has show-desktop, the panel's Show Desktop button. flickos-menu 1.6 has
# Quick Settings (`flickos-menu quick`), which the volume and battery icons
# and Super+A open while it is on. 1.10 has the phone popup (`flickos-menu
# phone`), which the phone button opens while the phone connection is on.
# flickos-shortcuts 1.16 reads the merged files while the labwc-merge marker
# exists (an older sheet would show only the user's keys).
Breaks: flick-tiler (<< 1.7),
        flickos-menu (<< 1.10),
        flickos-shortcuts (<< 1.16)
# waypaper: the chooser's Wallpaper button (shown only when it is installed).
Recommends: waypaper
Description: FlickOS desktop layouts and styles, and the flickos-layout tool
 Desktop layouts for the FlickOS labwc session: Redmond (one bottom panel),
 Cupertino (top bar and an auto-hiding dock) and Traditional (top panel and
 window list), each with its panel arrangement and window title bar
 buttons. Dark (Arc-Dark) and Light (Arc) styles recolor GTK apps, icons,
 window borders, panel, terminal, launcher and notifications, and each has
 its own wallpaper. A user's own wallpaper (waypaper) is kept. Desktop
 clicks choose what a left or right click on the empty desktop does. Quick
 Settings, when turned on, opens from the panel's volume and battery icons
 and Super+A. The phone button opens the phone popup while the phone
 connection is on, and the fuzzel menu otherwise.
 flickos-layout lists the layouts and styles, applies a choice to the
 running session and starts the panel and notifications at login. The
 Desktop Layout & Style chooser (Settings menu and app launcher) shows each
 layout with a preview.
 .
 The choice is applied through generated files in $XDG_RUNTIME_DIR, so
 nothing is copied into the home directory and package updates keep
 reaching every user.
